  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive).\n\nUSAGE:\nOften used in the ている form to describe a state. The noun form くびれ refers to a narrow waist or indentation, and is commonly used when talking about body shape (e.g., ウエストのくびれ, a slim waistline).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ウエストがくびれる (to have a narrow waist)\n- {真|ま}ん{中|なか}がくびれる (to be pinched in at the middle)\n- くびれた{形|かたち} (a pinched/hourglass shape)",
